.KEY x
.BRA {
.KET }
;
; Device level, no DOS and no filesystem (sdcard.md sec.10).
;
; Everything measured so far went through DOS and FAT. If the device alone is
; already about 1 MB/s then that is the medium and there is no loss to find
; above it; if it is much faster, the loss is between the device and the file.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[raw] device-level reads"
SDRaw 4 4 >DEBUG:
SDRaw 16 8 >DEBUG:
SDRaw 64 8 >DEBUG:
SDRaw 256 8 >DEBUG:
Echo >DEBUG: "[raw] and the same again, to separate cold from warm"
SDRaw 64 8 >DEBUG:
SDRaw 4 4 >DEBUG:
Echo >DEBUG: "[raw] done"
